  "notes": "West leads the ♥J which South wins. South has 11 top tricks (2 spades, 2 hearts, 3 diamonds, and 4 clubs). Only the spade suit offers hope for trick 12.\n\nSouth should cash the ♠A or ♠K from his hand and lead a low spade towards North's ♠J. If West follows low, the ♠J should be played. The ♠J will be worth a trick whenever the ♠Q is in the West hand. If the ♠J loses to East's ♠Q, the contract will still make if spades break 3-3.\n\nCashing a top spade honour first gives South the slight extra chance that East was dealt a singleton ♠Q.\n\nNotice that leading the ♠J from North can never help. If East has the ♠Q, he will simply cover the ♠J. Leading the ♠J will work only when spades are 3-3. The recommended line will also work in this case.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♥J which South wins. South has 11 top tricks (2 spades, 2 hearts, 3 diamonds, and 4 clubs). Only the spade suit offers hope for trick 12.",
